<title>SOUTH AFRICA: No immediate job cuts seen at Vaal Reefs.</title>
<headline>No immediate job cuts seen at Vaal Reefs.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd said on Thursday it had no immediate plans to cut jobs at its Vaal Reefs Exploration and Mining Co unit.</p>
<p>&quot;No retrenchments are immediately contemplated although some redeployment of employees at No 3 shaft is likely,&quot; Anglo said.</p>
<p>Earlier Vaal Reefs mine manager David Fisher had said the mine would have to make major job cuts.</p>
<p>&quot;We will have to investigate compulsory retrenchments...we will have to make fairly significant reductions,&quot; Fisher said a presentation.</p>
<p>Anglo said that if productivity could be improved, retrenchment would not be necessary.</p>
<p>Vaal Reefs produced 16,022 kg of gold in the three months to end-March.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
